WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.530
Joe: From calorie count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:04.422
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.422 --> 00:00:06.900
between Quiznos in the UK and the US.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.595
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.920
In the UK, Quiznos sandwiches
come in four sizes.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:16.090
Firstly, we have the kids' size,

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.850
which is 4 1/2 inches.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.460
Then we have a small
sub, which is 6 inches.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.825
A medium sub from a UK
Quiznos is 9 inches,

00:00:22.825 --> 00:00:24.317
or at least it should
be before we got hungry

00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:25.890
and ate it by mistake.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.140
And then, finally, we have a large sub,

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.280
which is 12 inches, or 1 foot long.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.290
In the US, our Quiznos
sandwiches come in four sizes:

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:37.079
the Sammie, a 4 inch, an
8 inch, and a 12 inch.

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:39.587
And I want to give Quiznos
props for not calling this,

00:00:39.587 --> 00:00:42.610
like, a sandwich taco or
something really obnoxious.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:44.860
Also in the US at a Quiznos,
you can get party platters

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.220
of either 20 3-inch sandwiches

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:49.970
or 14 flatbreads cut in half.

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:51.810
There are no fountain drinks
at a Quiznos in the UK.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:53.440
Instead, we just have cans and bottles,

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.456
which are 330 milliliters and
500 milliliters, respectively.

00:00:57.456 --> 00:00:58.655
In the US at a Quiznos,

00:00:58.655 --> 00:01:00.560
you can get your drinks in three sizes.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.330
Either a bottle, which is 20 ounces;

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:04.210
the regular, also 20 ounces;

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:06.596
or the large, which they did not have.

00:01:06.596 --> 00:01:08.263
Harry: Let's weigh a
classic Italian foot-long

00:01:08.263 --> 00:01:11.370
from a Quiznos in the UK
to see what it comes to.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.606
So, our scales could
just about handle that.

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:15.160
It turns out that a
foot-long classic Italian

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:18.238
from a UK Quiznos is 520 grams.

00:01:18.238 --> 00:01:22.362
Joe: In the US, Quiznos'
classic foot-long Italian is ...

00:01:22.362 --> 00:01:26.142
about, like, 460?

00:01:26.142 --> 00:01:27.520
[burps]

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.120
Quiznos was one of the first
chains to toast their subs,

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:33.110
so now let's arbitrarily
compare the toastedness

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:35.003
between our bread and the UK bread.

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:39.410
In our extremely precise
comparison metric,

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:40.923
it looks like the US maybe has the edge

00:01:40.923 --> 00:01:42.700
when it comes to toastiness of the bread.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.640
The inside of this is completely soggy,

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.390
and the outside, just very average.

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:50.460
Here is everything you'll
only find on the menu

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.350
at a Quiznos in the UK.

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:57.350
And here are a lot of the
USA Quiznos' exclusive items.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.116
Let's start with some
sandwich options first.

00:02:00.116 --> 00:02:01.716
The first one is this one.

00:02:01.716 --> 00:02:04.162
It's a vegan pakora sandwich.

00:02:04.162 --> 00:02:05.730
Pakora's an Indian food which is made of

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:07.190
chopped and spiced onions,

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:09.430
and opening this, I got a real hit

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:11.330
of some really nice flavors, actually.

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:17.610
It's actually really good. Very flavorful.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:18.930
Next up, we've got one which I'm surprised

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.765
wasn't on the US menu, which is a BLT.

00:02:21.765 --> 00:02:23.590
You can also get peri-peri
chicken from a UK Quiznos.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:25.090
Peri-peri chicken is just, like, a kind of

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.660
chili-marinated chicken

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:28.050
which has a little bit of heat to it.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.500
Another slightly surprising exclusive,

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.430
in that I'm surprised you
don't have it in the US,

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:32.810
is the barbecue chicken.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.030
They've given us a small sub,

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:35.988
but it looks like they've
written "smell" on it,

00:02:35.988 --> 00:02:37.640
so [sniffs].

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:38.473
For the meat lovers,

00:02:38.473 --> 00:02:40.520
we have a barbecue
steak and pepperoni sub.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:41.790
Then we have a classic British filling,

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.710
which is this one: ham,
cheese, and pickle.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:44.630
Now, when we say pickle here,

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.940
we don't mean slices of pickled cucumber.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:48.098
What we mean is pickle,

00:02:48.098 --> 00:02:50.300
which is a brown, vinegary condiment

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.362
made with various vegetables.

00:02:52.362 --> 00:02:53.854
Oh, no, they actually do mean pickle.

00:02:53.854 --> 00:02:56.095
[laughing]

00:02:56.095 --> 00:02:57.510
They mean actual pickle!

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.270
Next up we've got the Zesty Steak sub.

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:00.980
I'm not exactly sure
what makes this zesty,

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:03.030
so I'm gonna try it and try and find out.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.050
I'd be lying if I said

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:07.400
this was the zestiest
thing I've ever eaten.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.990
There's some kind of,
like, salsa on the top,

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:10.770
which I guess is supposed
to be the zesty component,

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:14.070
but basically not much
flavor coming from it.

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:15.730
Perhaps the meatiest
option on the whole menu

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:17.210
is the 3 Meat Stack.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.543
So, it looks as if the three meats

00:03:18.543 --> 00:03:20.351
are ham, bacon, and beef.

00:03:20.351 --> 00:03:22.658
But there's also some olives
in there, some lettuce,

00:03:22.658 --> 00:03:24.102
tomato, and cheese.

00:03:24.102 --> 00:03:25.850
And then, lastly, we have
a double cheese melt.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:28.475
This is basically just a
grilled cheese, but in sub form.

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:31.990
The Chipotle turkey on wheat.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:33.500
Eh, looks all right.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.458
The honey bacon --

00:03:34.458 --> 00:03:36.133
oh, there's honey in this, dude!

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:38.210
A honey bacon club.

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:39.480
Yeah, I can get down on that.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:43.768
The Southwest chicken,
on their jalapeño bread.

00:03:43.768 --> 00:03:44.776
[fight sounds]

00:03:44.776 --> 00:03:47.210
Eh, I don't know, that one
looks kind of rough in there.

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:49.620
This veggie sandwich is
packed with veggies, man.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.810
Veggie on wheat, for all
you health nuts out there.

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:53.920
The black Angus.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:54.800
This one ...

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.200
I don't know about this one.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:04:00.250
I think having black Angus,
I guess, like, shaved steak?

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:02.260
Ooh, the spicy Monterey.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:06.200
Turkey club, overflowing
with turkey clubiness.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.427
Next up we have toasties.

00:04:07.427 --> 00:04:09.610
Now, toasties are a very
popular lunch snack in the UK.

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:11.460
It's what we call a grilled cheese.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:13.210
So if you go to the UK
and ask for a toastie,

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:14.043
that's what you'll get.

00:04:14.043 --> 00:04:15.760
Toasties at Quiznos come in the form of

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:18.743
cheese, ham and cheese, and tuna mayo.

00:04:18.743 --> 00:04:22.241
In the US, you can get a
Quiznos sandwich in Sammie form.

00:04:22.241 --> 00:04:24.560
And what that kind of looks like is a --

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:25.440
I don't know if it's a pita bread,

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:26.530
but it's kind of folded over.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:27.496
You saw it earlier.

00:04:27.496 --> 00:04:30.170
Could we go for the instant
replay of the Sammie?

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:31.003
That thing.

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:33.060
You can't get those in the
UK, from my understanding.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:36.757
And I don't know if you can
get every sandwich Sammied.

00:04:36.757 --> 00:04:40.220
You can get the classic
Italian, the black Angus,

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:42.762
the lobster, and the slow-roasted chicken.

00:04:42.762 --> 00:04:44.540
I have to say, like, I
thought it was stupid,

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:46.860
but this actually, like,
looks more manageable

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:48.070
if you just want to try something out.

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:50.115
It's been sitting for a while, but, like,

00:04:50.115 --> 00:04:51.780
looks a little bit like a gordita.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:53.250
Next up we've got crispy chicken fillets.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:55.410
These are basically just breaded
and fried chicken tenders,

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:58.310
and they come in portions
of four, six, or eight.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:04:59.143
On the side in the UK,

00:04:59.143 --> 00:05:01.100
you can get a portion of criss-cut fries.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.900
These come as small or large,

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.290
and they're just potato that's
cut into a crisscross pattern

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:06.660
and deep-fried.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.952
Our last hot side option is garlic bread.

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:12.628
It looks like it's made
with the same bread

00:05:12.628 --> 00:05:14.362
that Quiznos uses for most
of their subs in the UK.

00:05:14.362 --> 00:05:16.130
However, there's some garlic
butter spread on top of it,

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:17.510
and then it's toasted as well.

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:19.640
You can also get this with cheese.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:22.923
Tater tots in the US

00:05:22.923 --> 00:05:26.647
of a regular and jalapeño bacon.

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:30.673
Yeah. Whoa.

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:34.623
I bit right into a jalapeño.

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:39.420
OK. Slow down, Joe.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:40.280
Pizza time.

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:41.113
Peter: Pizza time.

00:05:41.113 --> 00:05:43.190
In the UK, Quiznos
offers a range of pizzas.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:44.320
We're going to go through them one by one

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.730
to show you what they are.

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:46.910
Let's start with this one.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:48.800
Now, this one is the chicken Baja,

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:51.148
which is a barbecue-sauce-based pizza

00:05:51.148 --> 00:05:53.506
with some bacon, some barbecue chicken,

00:05:53.506 --> 00:05:56.440
some kind of Baja sauce, I presume,

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:57.660
and some red onion as well.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:00.230
Our next pizza option is
the peri-peri chicken.

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:01.170
This one's pretty straightforward.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:04.040
It's peri-peri chicken,
peppers, and onions.

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:06.250
From there, we're moving
on to the veggie supreme.

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:07.570
This is a vegetarian-friendly option

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:10.530
with some peppers, mushrooms,
onions, and olives.

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:12.740
Then we're moving on to
the barbecue chicken pizza.

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:14.256
This one has a barbecue-sauce base,

00:06:14.256 --> 00:06:15.356
some barbecue chicken,

00:06:15.356 --> 00:06:17.400
and then, once again, peppers and onions.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:19.192
I personally hate it when
they use barbecue sauce

00:06:19.192 --> 00:06:20.790
as the base instead of tomato sauce.

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:23.150
Like, it ain't broke, don't fix it.

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:24.233
Then, finally, we have the classics,

00:06:24.233 --> 00:06:25.570
Margherita and pepperoni.

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:27.114
Really not much to say about these.

00:06:27.114 --> 00:06:29.597
[Italian folk music plays]

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:33.480
Quiznos in the UK also offers
a range of wraps and salads.

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:36.040
The following things can
be used in either form:

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:39.320
Chicken Caesar, barbecue
chicken and ranch, tuna,

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:41.350
honey mustard chicken, peri-peri chicken,

00:06:41.350 --> 00:06:43.220
and Mediterranean salad.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:44.445
Soups.

00:06:44.445 --> 00:06:46.011
What is this, chili?

00:06:46.953 --> 00:06:47.786
Chili?

00:06:47.786 --> 00:06:48.668
Ooh, cheddar bro --

00:06:48.668 --> 00:06:50.560
I don't even gotta open this
to know it's cheddar broccoli.

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:52.017
Sorry, dude.

00:06:52.017 --> 00:06:52.850
[fart sound effect]

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:53.975
Yeah. Ugh.

00:06:53.975 --> 00:06:57.091
It's not that this is a
bad version of the soup,

00:06:57.091 --> 00:06:59.450
it's that cheddar broccoli,
or cheese broccoli,

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:02.130
I mean, this smells exactly like a fart.

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:04.750
And everyone's favorite, chicken noodle.

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:06.533
Salads.

00:07:06.533 --> 00:07:08.800
You can get a side garden salad.

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:10.670
The lobster is supposed to
be, like, a thing for them,

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:13.272
so you can also get lobster salad.

00:07:13.272 --> 00:07:14.647
See that?

00:07:14.647 --> 00:07:16.200
Actually looks pretty good.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.585
This is the, uh, I think the chef salad.

00:07:19.585 --> 00:07:21.123
The Italian salad, which I think is

00:07:21.123 --> 00:07:23.348
everything that comes
on the Italian sandwich

00:07:23.348 --> 00:07:24.820
thrown in a bowl.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:26.840
And then finally we
have some snack options.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:29.670
Quiznos in the UK offers
these Real-branded crisps,

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:32.320
which come as sea salt or
cheese and onion flavor.

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:35.570
We can get a fruit and oat
cookie from a UK Quiznos.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:37.830
The packaging advertises
this as a "giant" cookie,

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:39.790
but to me this is just
a regular-sized cookie.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:42.290
So I don't know if all
the workers at Paterson's

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:43.610
are just very small

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:46.150
or if they need to
change their terminology.

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:47.678
And, finally, we have two muffin options,

00:07:47.678 --> 00:07:49.410
chocolate or blueberry.

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:52.889
These fantastic chips are
available at Quiznos in the US.

00:07:52.889 --> 00:07:54.830
Miss Vickie has a bunch
of different brands.

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:56.190
On top of that, at Quiznos,

00:07:56.190 --> 00:07:59.960
you can get so many other types of chips.

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:02.103
Let's get a few of those
on the screen right now.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:07.210
Quiznos in the US: We
got your chips covered.

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:09.166
Getting great audio,
[chip bag rustling]

00:08:09.166 --> 00:08:10.249
'cause I put this
[chip bag rustling]

00:08:10.249 --> 00:08:12.749
right in front of the mic.
[chip bag rustling]

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:16.810
Unfortunately, Quiznos in the UK

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:18.630
doesn't disclose any of its
nutritional information.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:19.880
So I'm just gonna sit here and, like,

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:21.280
think about Pokémon, I guess.

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:25.860
What's Pokémon?

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:28.650
At a Quiznos in the US, a
classic Italian 12-inch sub

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.640
is 1,260 calories.

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:33.730
63 grams of fat, 22
grams of saturated fat,

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:36.655
3,760 milligrams of sodium,

00:08:36.655 --> 00:08:38.850
and 115 grams of carbs.

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:41.980
If you're worried about
sodium, I got some bad news.

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:46.930
Throw in a bag of the lovely
Miss Vickie's sea salt chips,

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:48.113
arguably the best flavor

00:08:48.113 --> 00:08:49.846
of Miss Vickie's chips, the sea salt.

00:08:49.846 --> 00:08:51.330
It's like, sea salt and who cares?

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:52.210
Love these chips.

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:54.561
And a large Coke.

00:08:54.561 --> 00:08:55.810
Yes, I'm aware that's a regular,

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:57.770
can we get someone in
post to make that bigger?

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:58.860
Thank you.

00:08:58.860 --> 00:08:59.901
Add these two things,

00:08:59.901 --> 00:09:03.476
and now your meal is 2,040 calories,

00:09:03.476 --> 00:09:06.710
84 grams of fat, 25 of
those grams saturated,

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:09.451
4,290 milligrams of sodium,

00:09:09.451 --> 00:09:13.392
and 264 grams of carbos.

00:09:13.392 --> 00:09:15.180
For those of you with a sweet tooth,

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:18.405
if you want to substitute
the chips for a cookie --

00:09:18.405 --> 00:09:19.538
for a cookie --

00:09:19.538 --> 00:09:21.905
[comedic music]

00:09:26.228 --> 00:09:27.115
[sighs]

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:30.060
For a cookie [clears throat].

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:31.610
Now that you've got the
cookie instead of the chips,

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:32.800
with the large Coke still,

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:35.725
you're going to go up to 2,133 calories,

00:09:35.725 --> 00:09:37.000
81 grams of fat,

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:40.025
33 grams of saturated fat,

00:09:40.025 --> 00:09:41.783
4,100 milligrams of sodium,

00:09:41.783 --> 00:09:45.078
and 279 grams of carbs.

00:09:45.078 --> 00:09:47.770
[birds chirping]

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:49.925
Is it au jus or au juice?

00:09:49.925 --> 00:09:51.033
Au jus?

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.190
Ad: This life-saving device stops --

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:57.910
Are you f---ing kidding me?
This video is two seconds long.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:59.185
Great, thanks guys.

00:09:59.185 --> 00:10:00.818
Video: Au jus, French.

00:10:00.818 --> 00:10:01.760
Au jus?

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:04.593
In the US, a French dip, 12 inch, with

00:10:04.593 --> 00:10:06.890
au jus, right?

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:10.481
Is 1,140 calories, 45 grams of fat,

00:10:10.481 --> 00:10:12.070
14 saturated fat,

00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:14.661
3,370 milligrams of sodium,

00:10:14.661 --> 00:10:16.369
and 119 carbs.

00:10:16.369 --> 00:10:18.620
Now, Conner, I gotta get
personal for a second here.

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:20.553
The last time I ate at a Quiznos

00:10:20.553 --> 00:10:22.611
was probably 12 years ago.

00:10:22.611 --> 00:10:24.900
I worked in an office
job that I really hated,

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:26.951
and in the lobby was a Quiznos.

00:10:26.951 --> 00:10:29.440
And I went there one day with
a coworker, got a sandwich,

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:31.697
and on the way out, that
coworker said to me,

00:10:31.697 --> 00:10:32.830
"What'd you think?"

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:34.797
And I believe my exact words were,

00:10:34.797 --> 00:10:37.160
"You'd have to pay me to
eat at Quiznos again."

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:39.127
12 years later,

00:10:39.127 --> 00:10:40.743
they're paying me to eat at Quiznos.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:48.950
Dude. This is pretty good.

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:51.680
This is not the most calorific
sandwich on a Quiznos menu.

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:53.330
That distinguished honor goes to

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:55.500
the 12-inch Italian meatball.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:59.603
It's 1,390 calories for
one 12-inch sandwich.

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:05.040
This sandwich is pretty good.

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:06.980
This dipping thing, this don't work.

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:08.740
I don't want this cold dip
coming with my sandwich

00:11:08.740 --> 00:11:10.810
when I get home, I don't want
to do all this in the Quiznos,

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:12.880
and I certainly can't do this in the car.

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:14.470
Quiznos, listen to me,

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:17.884
I'm about to give you
a million-dollar idea.

00:11:17.884 --> 00:11:18.833
So check this out.

00:11:18.833 --> 00:11:21.074
You guys, with some food science,

00:11:21.074 --> 00:11:23.390
do what the McGriddle did. Right?

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:25.830
With the syrup in their pancake buns.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:26.818
You do the same thing.

00:11:26.818 --> 00:11:30.900
You inject this juice into
the bread of the sandwich,

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:32.315
so it's all in one.

00:11:32.315 --> 00:11:34.390
That'd be amazing, dude. I
would totally get the sandwich.

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:35.300
Is this not a bad idea?

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:36.370
No dipping, right?

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:38.440
I just saved the brand. You're welcome.

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:41.240
I think I deserve a Quiznos black card.

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:42.970
Now, our American audience
might be wondering,

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:44.730
"Quiznos, didn't they go out of business?"

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:46.250
And the answer is, not really.

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:48.090
And apparently they might
be making a comeback.

00:11:48.090 --> 00:11:52.471
Research on the brand shows
that between 2007 and 2017,

00:11:52.471 --> 00:11:55.487
Quiznos went from 4,700 US locations

00:11:55.487 --> 00:11:56.937
to fewer than 400.

00:11:56.937 --> 00:11:59.270
They had a fierce competitor
in Subway, Jimmy John's,

00:11:59.270 --> 00:12:01.190
and several other small sandwich chains.

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:02.987
They were hit hard by the Great Recession

00:12:02.987 --> 00:12:05.086
and had to deal with several lawsuits

00:12:05.086 --> 00:12:07.677
from many of their own franchisees.

00:12:07.677 --> 00:12:08.710
Ooh.

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:10.260
In 2014, Quiznos actually filed

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:11.918
for Chapter 11 bankruptcy in the US,

00:12:11.918 --> 00:12:14.177
but it looks like some of
their stores stuck around.

00:12:14.177 --> 00:12:16.550
According to a recent article
we found in QSR Magazine,

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:18.350
which does read awfully
like a press release,

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:21.410
Quiznos is "moving forward
with new designs, menu items,

00:12:21.410 --> 00:12:24.000
and drive-thrus," so perhaps
the future is bright.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.066
Hate to break it to you,

00:12:25.066 --> 00:12:27.650
all these sandwich places
are almost exactly the same.

00:12:27.650 --> 00:12:29.735
So there's no reason why Quiznos can't be

00:12:29.735 --> 00:12:31.520
just as popular as any other ones, right?

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.974
Especially now, like,
doing kind of a comeback.

00:12:33.974 --> 00:12:35.050
What they have to do --

00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:37.420
pay attention, Quiznos, more
information coming your way.

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:38.644
What Quiznos has to do

00:12:38.644 --> 00:12:41.020
is go after each sandwich
chain individually

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:44.187
and just position
themselves as not being that

00:12:44.187 --> 00:12:45.490
and picking the thing that sucks about it

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.870
and just being like,
hey, we don't have that.

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:48.210
Like, you want to beat Subway?

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:51.060
"Quiznos: Yoga-mat-material-free
in the bread."

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:52.409
There you go. Give me
another sandwich place.

00:12:52.409 --> 00:12:53.992
This is easy. Go on, give me one.

00:12:53.992 --> 00:12:55.510
Jimmy John's -- dude,
correct me if I'm wrong,

00:12:55.510 --> 00:12:56.970
but, like, Jimmy John's,
their whole thing was, like,

00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:58.978
they make sandwiches super fast, right?

00:12:58.978 --> 00:13:00.576
In order to do that, it's like,

00:13:00.576 --> 00:13:02.030
one person slices the bread,

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:03.670
then the next person cuts the meat, right?

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:04.880
And the next person
adds the cheese, right?

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:06.346
It's like, five people touch your sandwich

00:13:06.346 --> 00:13:07.812
to make it go faster.

00:13:07.812 --> 00:13:10.340
"Quiznos: Your sandwich won't be touched

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:12.290
by five stoned teenagers."

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:16.212
Potbelly's? Nobody wants
to eat in an antique store.

00:13:16.212 --> 00:13:18.420
"Quiznos: Our furniture
isn't a hundred years old."

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:19.495
What's left?

00:13:20.487 --> 00:13:22.330
Oh, Jersey Mike's?

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:25.013
"Quiznos: We're not from New Jersey."

00:13:25.013 --> 00:13:27.213
[jazzy music plays]

